---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const lastUpdated = 'August 9, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={`Privacy policy for ${SITE.name}.`}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <p>
        This policy explains what happens with your data when you visit {SITE.name}
        ({SITE.url}), operated by {SITE.legalName}.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect today</h2>
      <p>
        As of the date above, {SITE.name} does <strong>not</strong> use any analytics or
        advertising cookies, does not require an account, and has no forms that collect personal
        data. The site's search box runs entirely in your browser and never sends your search terms
        to a server.
      </p>
      <p>
        The only thing stored locally on your device is your cookie-banner choice (accept/decline),
        kept in your browser's local storage so we don't ask again on every visit. See our
        <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>What may change</h2>
      <p>
        If {SITE.name} adds analytics in the future (for example, to understand which guides are
        most useful), it will only run after you actively accept cookies via the banner, and this
        policy — along with the <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> — will be updated first to
        disclose exactly what's collected and why.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted by Vercel Inc., which processes standard technical data (like IP
        addresses) as part of serving any website, under its own privacy policy. Links to external
        sites (airport authorities, transport operators, etc.) are provided for convenience; once
        you leave {SITE.name}, that site's own privacy policy applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Since we don't currently collect or store personal data beyond the local cookie-consent
        choice described above, there is generally nothing to access, correct, or delete on our
        end. If that changes, this section will be updated to explain how to exercise your rights
        (access, rectification, deletion, and objection) over any data we hold.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
